<title>USA: Alliance World sets period for tender offer.</title>
<headline>Alliance World sets period for tender offer.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alliance World Dollar Government Fund Inc said on Wednesday the board of directors has fixed the 12 consecutive week period ending Friday, August 29, 1997, for determining whether the fund will buy back its common stock.</p>
<p>The fund is to commence a tender offer during the fourth quarter of 1997, if the fund's common stock trades at an average discount of five percent or more from its net asset value, Alliance World said.</p>
<p>As of the close of trading on June 20, 1997, the fund's shares were trading at a discount to net asset value of 3.74 percent.</p>
</text>
